  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 114 AM MDT TUE OCT 27 2026\nAs the next trough approaches our area Friday, precipitation chances \nwill begin to increase across higher terrain in SW-Idaho Friday \nafternoon. This will ring true come Saturday afternoon, except \nprecipitation chances will continue to increase through the day \nSunday (mainly across southwest Idaho) as the trough and it's \nassociated cold front cross the area. The southwesterly flow aloft \nwill keep snow levels at 5-7 kft MSL (rising as you move from west \nto east). This should keep the majority of snow accumulations above\n6kft MSL (a 30-50% chance of exceeding 2 inches of snow Saturday\nafternoon through Sunday, chances increasing with elevation). \nWhile snow levels lower following the frontal passage, this will\nalso be about the time precipitation begins tapering off. The \narea will dry out Monday as upper level ridging builds in behind\nthe departing trough. Dry conditions will prevail through the \nbeginning of next week. Seasonable or below normal temperatures \nwill continue through the long-term period.",
